From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <noreply@xe.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:19:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/50] direct route: revoke pending copies on site change; re-check ownership on completion

A copy result is handed to the renderer only if, when it completes, the
guest is still owned by the caller (the same check as for issuing it), is
on the same frame sink, and its main page has not changed site since the
copy was requested; otherwise the copy is requested again (with a new
ownership check) or the stream ends.

When the guest's main page changes site (WebContentsObserver::
PrimaryPageChanged), the source's copies not yet drawn are cancelled in viz
(CancelKeyedCopyOutputRequests) and requested again for the new page;
cancellations do not count as failures.

Re-embedding: viz already drops a request whose target surface now has a
different embed token (CompositorFrameSinkSupport::TakeCopyOutputRequests
sends kEmbeddingTokenChanged, or never takes it), so a parked request
cannot be drawn after the guest is attached elsewhere; the source then
retries with a new ownership check.

Covered by ControlledFrameTextureSourceTest.Lifetime (cross-site navigation
continues with the new page; removal and renderer crash end the stream).
---
